sweet ufs: log progress from a thread that never prints

The console and the log flusher both stop on some boots while the machine
is alive: bp14 printed up to "Early boot complete" (8.9 s) and then froze,
yet the modem thread's 150 s timer still returned the phone to recovery.
Two things made that unreadable.  The flusher printed on a write error, so
a wedged console could take the only path that persists the log with it,
and every progress line went through printf (), so the ring held nothing
from the moment the console stopped.

Drop the flusher's error printf (fails/ferr are in the ring instead), and
add a kick thread that appends one line every two seconds with the ring
total, flush sequence, flusher wakeups, last error, the age of the
flusher's current iteration, the command serial and the UFS lock state.
It never touches the console, so after a "frozen" boot the ring shows
whether the disk and the flusher kept running (console wedge) or
everything stopped together.

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
